Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "path": locate files that look like manifest files (e.g. composer.json, package.json)  
  – "id": join‐key to reach the actual file body in SAMPLE_CONTENTS  

• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "sample_path": same purpose as “path”; lets you filter to JSON manifests without a join  
  – "content": full text of each file – parse this JSON to reach the require/dependencies section  
  – "sample_repo_name": helps aggregate results per repository  
  – "id": optional join‐key back to SAMPLE_FILES if needed  

Typical filter conditions  
    WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'  
    WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json'  
    WHERE TRY_PARSE_JSON("content") IS NOT NULL  

Below are ten Snowflake SQL snippets – each limited to 20 rows – moving from very simple exploration toward the logic you would finally use to count package names in a “require” section.  All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at distinct manifest paths that appear to be Composer files
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_path"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Same idea for NPM package manifests (package.json)
SELECT DISTINCT "sample_path"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Peek at one Composer manifest’s raw JSON to confirm structure
SELECT "sample_repo_name",
       "sample_path",
       "content"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Parse the JSON and pull back ONLY the “require” object as VARIANT
SELECT "sample_repo_name",
       PARSE_JSON("content"):"require"        AS "require_obj"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
  AND TRY_PARSE_JSON("content") IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Flatten the require object to list each package‑name / version pair
SELECT t."sample_repo_name",
       f.key            AS "package_name",
       f.value::STRING  AS "required_version"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require" ) f
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
  AND TRY_PARSE_JSON(t."content") IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Count how many times each package shows up across all sampled Composer files
SELECT f.key                               AS "package_name",
       COUNT(*)                            AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require" ) f
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
  AND TRY_PARSE_JSON(t."content") IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY f.key
ORDER BY "occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Same exploration for package.json ➜ “dependencies” instead of “require”
SELECT f.key                    AS "package_name",
       COUNT(*)                 AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"dependencies" ) f
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%package.json'
  AND TRY_PARSE_JSON(t."content") IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY f.key
ORDER BY "occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Show Composer packages that start with “symfony/”
SELECT f.key                             AS "symfony_pkg",
       COUNT(*)                          AS "cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require" ) f
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
  AND TRY_PARSE_JSON(t."content") IS NOT NULL
  AND f.key ILIKE 'symfony/%'
GROUP BY f.key
ORDER BY "cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Per‑repository list of required packages (Composer)
SELECT t."sample_repo_name",
       f.key             AS "package_name",
       f.value::STRING   AS "version_constraint"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => PARSE_JSON(t."content"):"require" ) f
WHERE t."sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
  AND TRY_PARSE_JSON(t."content") IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY t."sample_repo_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Comprehensive frequency list of Composer “require” packages (most complete query)
SELECT f.key                    AS "package_name",
       COUNT(*)                 AS "freq"
FROM (
       SELECT "content"
       FROM   GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
       WHERE  "sample_path" ILIKE '%composer.json'
         AND  TRY_PARSE_JSON("content") IS NOT NULL
     ) c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => PARSE_JSON(c."content"):"require" ) f
GROUP BY f.key
ORDER BY "freq" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Each successive query builds insight into how the JSON manifests are stored, how to extract the “require”/“dependencies” section, how to flatten those objects, and finally how to count package names across all sampled repositories.
